# the package is installed for tests; a root conftest papering over that is not tracked
/conftest.py
# No runtime state is written inside this tree any more: the audit log, the
# privacy-skill KG, the Art. 33(2) breach log and the pseudonymisation session
# store all resolve under the OS user-state home (audit_log._user_state_home),
# outside this tree entirely, and the credential and evidence-pack paths went
# with the modules 2.0.0 removed. So the rules that covered them are gone.
#
# These two stay, for the opposite reason to the others. Nothing writes them any
# more, but 1.x runs left real files at both paths on working trees that have
# been around since before the split: a credential master key, and generated
# evidence packs. Without the rules the next `git add -A` commits them — which
# is not hypothetical, both were caught in the index on this branch and taken
# back out. Leave the rules until the stale files are deleted from the working
# trees that still carry them.
src/privacy_shield/user/.credentials_master.key
src/privacy_shield/compliance_evidence/
